{"name":"Aspen Mist","hex":"#cfd7cb","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aspen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to the aspen tree.","Tremulous, trembling."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A poplar tree, especially of section Populus sect. Populus, of medium-size trees with thin, straight trunks of a greenish-white color.","The wood of such a tree; usually pale, lightweight and soft."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspen"},{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aspen","blocks":[{"text":"Aspen is a common name for certain tree species in the Populus sect. Populus, of the Populus (poplar) genus.\nAspens were referred to as \"asps\" in earlier forms of English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Snowbowlaspens.jpg/330px-Snowbowlaspens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aspen","wikidata":"Q1087592"},{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%